    <!-- Section 10: Measuring AI Search Performance -->
    <section>
      <h2>Measuring AI Search Performance</h2>

      <p>Measuring AI search performance differs fundamentally from tracking traditional SEO metrics. There is no equivalent of Google Search Console for AI citations &mdash; yet. However, effective measurement is achievable through a combination of manual monitoring and emerging tooling.</p>

      <h3>Manual Citation Tracking</h3>

      <p>The most reliable method for tracking AI search visibility is structured manual testing. Run target queries across ChatGPT, Perplexity, Copilot, and Google (for AIO) and record whether the business is cited. Key query categories to monitor for a Birmingham business:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Brand name queries (e.g., "tell me about [business name] Birmingham")</li>
        <li>Core service + location (e.g., "best [service] in Birmingham")</li>
        <li>Comparison queries (e.g., "[service A] vs [service B] Birmingham")</li>
        <li>Informational queries in the relevant niche (e.g., "how much does [service] cost in Birmingham")</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Execute these tests weekly and log outcomes systematically. Over time, patterns emerge: which platforms cite most frequently, which queries the business is absent from, and how visibility shifts as optimisation progresses.</p>

      <h3>Emerging Monitoring Tools</h3>

      <p>Several tools are emerging to automate AI search monitoring, including Otterly.ai, HubSpot's AI Search Grader, and custom scripts that query AI APIs and parse responses for brand mentions. While tooling is still maturing, early adoption provides Birmingham businesses with a data advantage over competitors that are not tracking AI visibility at all.</p>

      <h3>KPIs for AI Search</h3>

      <p>Our team recommends the following measurable KPIs for AI search optimisation programmes:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Citation frequency</strong> &mdash; how often the business is mentioned in AI answers for target queries. Track monthly.</li>
        <li><strong>Citation accuracy</strong> &mdash; whether the AI's description of the business is factually correct. Inaccurate citations can be more damaging than no citation at all.</li>
        <li><strong>Source link inclusion</strong> &mdash; whether the AI provides a link to the website alongside the citation. Linked citations drive traffic; unlinked citations drive brand awareness only.</li>
        <li><strong>Competitive share of voice</strong> &mdash; how citation frequency compares to Birmingham competitors for the same queries.</li>
        <li><strong>Referral traffic from AI sources</strong> &mdash; analytics data for traffic from chat.openai.com, perplexity.ai, and bing.com/chat domains.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

